  579:+      "deterministic_setup": [],
  580:+      "agent_guidance": "This artifact only ships org.springframework.boot.micrometer.metrics.test.autoconfigure.AutoConfigureMetrics and MetricsContextCustomizerFactory (+ nested DisableMetricsExportContextCustomizer). Without @AutoConfigureMetrics on a @SpringBootTest class, the customizer forces metrics export off for that test context; with it present, CompositeMeterRegistryAutoConfiguration/MetricsAutoConfiguration/SimpleMetricsExportAutoConfiguration/ObservationAutoConfiguration are auto-imported so a MeterRegistry (e.g. SimpleMeterRegistry) is actually registered. A meaningful test pair is: (1) a minimal @SpringBootTest WITHOUT the annotation asserting no usable MeterRegistry bean / metrics export is suppressed, and (2) one WITH @AutoConfigureMetrics asserting a MeterRegistry bean is present and records a meter. The underlying toggle is the plain Spring Boot property spring.test.metrics.export (default false, from spring-configuration-metadata.json) — this is ordinary @SpringBootTest(properties=...) test code, not host environment/system-property setup, so it does not need a deterministic_setup entry.",
