ngframework.boot.micrometer.metrics.test.autoconfigure.AutoConfigureMetrics and MetricsContextCustomizerFactory (+ nested DisableMetricsExportContextCustomizer). Without @AutoConfigureMetrics on a @SpringBootTest class, the customizer forces metrics export off for that test context; with it present, CompositeMeterRegistryAutoConfiguration/MetricsAutoConfiguration/SimpleMetricsExportAutoConfiguration/ObservationAutoConfiguration are auto-imported so a MeterRegistry (e.g. SimpleMeterRegistry) is actually registered. A meaningful test pair is: (1) a minimal @SpringBootTest WITHOUT the annotation asserting no usable MeterRegistry bean / metrics export is suppressed, and (2) one WITH @AutoConfigureMetrics asserting a MeterRegistry bean is present and records a meter. The underlying toggle is the plain Spring Boot property spring.test.metrics.export (default false, from spring-configuration-metadata.json) — this is ordinary @SpringBootTest(properties=...) test code, not host environment/system-property setup, so it does not need a deterministic_setup entry.\",\n581:+      \"risks\": [\n582:+        \"This is the first 'real' artifact in the spring-boot-*-test family to be onboarded here — its sibling POM-only starters (e.g. spring-boot-starter-micrometer-metrics-test) are already marked not-for-native-image with this artifact as the replacement, but there's no prior PR in this repo for a sibling like spring-boot-webmvc-test/spring-boot-restclient-test to cross-check the exact test shape against.\"\n583:+      ],\n584:+      \"applied_setup\": [],\n585:+      \"input_evidence\": [\n586:+        {\n587:+          \"name\": \"issue\",\n588:+          \"summary\": \"#9730 Support for org.springframework.boot:spring-boot-micrometer-metrics-test:4.1.1; label=library-new-request; body_chars=39\"\n589:+        },\n590:+        {\n591:+          \"name\": \"existing_tests\",\n592:+          \"summary\": \"0 existing test file path(s) included\"\n593:+        }\n594:+      ],\n595: