6-10-07T05:25:45.353123Z\",\n      \"library\": \"org.springframework.boot:spring-boot-micrometer-metrics-test:4.1.1\",\n      \"starting_commit\": \"a1faccbba8ef452ece56b70c2c839d22a6d270cb\",\n      \"ending_commit\": \"b806c425826b829eb140e9bb9677215f475ae75f\",\n      \"strategy_name\": \"optimistic_dynamic_access_iterative_pi_gpt-5.6-luna\",\n      \"agent\": \"pi\",\n      \"model\": \"gpt-5.6-luna\",\n      \"status\": \"failure\",\n      \"library_preparation_preflight\": {\n        \"status\": \"completed\",\n        \"action\": \"no_action\",\n        \"issue_number\": 9730,\n        \"issue_label\": \"library-new-request\",\n        \"library\": \"org.springframework.boot:spring-boot-micrometer-metrics-test:4.1.1\",\n        \"summary\": \"Pure test-support SPI module (one annotation + one ContextCustomizerFactory, registered via bundled META-INF/spring.factories). All classes it activates (MetricsAutoConfiguration, SimpleMetricsExportAutoConfiguration, CompositeMeterRegistryAutoConfiguration, ObservationAutoConfiguration) are already transitive compile dependencies via spring-boot-micrometer-metrics and spring-boot-micrometer-observation, declared on this artifact's own POM alongside spring-boot-test-autoconfigure and micrometer-observation-test. No Docker, external service, or environment/system property is required — it's an in-process Spring test-context customizer with zero network or native-OS surface.\",\n        \"deterministic_setup\": [],\n        \"agent_guidance\": \"This artifact only ships org.springframework.boot.micrometer.metrics.test.autoconfigure.AutoConfigureMetrics and MetricsContextCustomizerFactory (+ nested DisableMetricsExportContextCustomizer). Without @AutoConfigureMetrics on a @SpringBootTest class, the customizer forces metrics export off for that test context; with it present, CompositeMeterRegistryAutoConfiguration/MetricsAutoConfiguration/SimpleMetricsExportAutoConfiguration/ObservationAutoConfiguration are auto-imported so a MeterRegistry (e.g. SimpleMeterRegistry) is actually registered. A meaningful test pair is: (1) a minimal @SpringBootTest WITHOUT the annotation asserting no usable MeterRegistry bean / metrics export is suppressed, and (2) one WITH @AutoConfigureMetrics asserting a MeterRegistry bean is present and records a meter. The underlying toggle is the plain Spring Boot property spring.test.metrics.export (default false, from spring-configuration-metadata.json) — this is ordinary @SpringBootTest(properties=...) test code, not host environment/system-property setup, so it does not need a deterministic_setup entry.\",\n        \"risks\": [\n          \"This is the first 'real' artifact in the spring-boot-*-test family to be onboarded here — its sibling POM-only starters (e.g. spring-boot-starter-micrometer-metrics-test) are already marked not-for-native-image with this artifact as the replacement, but there's no prior PR in this repo for a sibling like spring-boot-webmvc-test/spring-boot-restclient-test to cross-check the exact test shape against.\"\n        ],\n        \"applied_setup\": [],\n        \"input_evidence\": [\n          {\n            \"name\": \"issue\",\n            \"summary\": \"#9730 Support for org.springframework.boot:spring-boot-micrometer-metrics-test:4.1.1; label=library-new-request; body_chars=39\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"name\": \"existing_tests\",\n            \"summary\": \"0 existing test file path(s) included\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"model\": \"sonnet\",\n        \"input_tokens_used\": 32,\n        \"output_tokens_used\": 14707\n      },\n      \"metrics\": {\n        \"input_tokens_used\": 501257,\n        \"cached_input_tokens_used\": 6648320,\n        \"output_tokens_used\": 51329,\n        \"iterations\": 12,\n        \"cost_usd\": 1.4741,\n        \"generated_loc\": 0,\n        \"tested_library_loc\": 0,\n        \"metadata_entries\": 0,\n        \"code_coverage_percent\": 0.0\n      },\n      \"artifacts\":